WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
In English, "I like" stays
the same: "I like football",

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:05.490
"I like sports".

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.410
But Lucía writes: Me gusta el fútbol.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.890
Then: Me gustan los deportes.

5
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.090
Same person.

6
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.250
Same liking.

7
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.810
Yet the verb has changed its ending.

8
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.330
If Lucía is the one doing the liking,

9
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.290
why does the verb change at all?

10
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.510
In this mission, you'll find
out what this verb really means,

11
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.060
and why the sentence
seems to flip round.

12
00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:29.390
You'll choose the little word
that shows who likes something,

13
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.330
and meet a verb that works the
same way: encantar, "to love".

14
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.180
Your mission: work out
why Lucía's verb changed.
